[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Scotch Game: Göring Gambit Declined"]
[ECO "C44"]
[Character "sharp,positional"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "counter-in-the-centre,give-back-material"]
[Kind "gambit"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 { White offers another pawn for a lead in development: the Göring Gambit. } 4... d5 { Do not take on c3. Hit back in the centre at once, so White's extra tempo has nothing to attack. }
5. exd5 5... Qxd5 { Takes back the pawn, and the queen is safe in the centre for now. }
6. cxd4 6... Bb4+ { A check first: White must block, and Black keeps control of d5. }
7. Nc3 7... Bg4 { Develops with a pin on the knight on f3, so White cannot use it freely. } 8. Be2 8... Bxf3 { Takes the knight that guards d4. } 9. Bxf3 9... Qc4 { Moves the queen with a threat on c3 and the bishop. Black has an equal game; plan: ...Nge7, ...O-O-O and trade queens if White allows it. } *
